Headless: follow a label's link

An app drawing labels itself has no QLabel to emit linkActivated, so a link in a label's rich text (send:, prompt:,
http(s): or Lua) did nothing in THeadlessSession, on the Android client or any other frontend with no window:
TLabel::slot_linkActivated() alone knew what a click on one does.

- TLabelModel gains followLink(), TLabel::slot_linkActivated()'s handling moved out of the widget: send: goes to the
  game through the aliases, prompt: to the main command line through the console frontend, http(s): through
  TAppFrontend::openWebPage(), a scheme that is neither and no Lua method call is noted in the Errors console with
  the same (TLabel-context) translation, and anything else runs as Lua. It says which it did, and linkScheme()
  reads a link's scheme as it does. visitLink() marks a link visited where the label has a visited colour, and
  linkTargets() reads a text's hrefs as QLabel reads them, so also a link containsAnchorTag() misses, as one with a
  raw < in its href. TLabel calls followLink() and visitLink(), and still gives the command line focus after a
  prompt: link; the desktop is unchanged.
- TNullConsoleFrontend::visitLabelLink() marks the link visited and restyles the label, as setLinkStyle() does, so
  the visited style changes labelContent().text and names the label in scriptWindowsChanged.
- THeadlessSession::followLabelLink(label, href) is the player's click: ran, or failed with errorString() for a Lua
  error, a link not run, a web link nothing opened and a prompt: link while the game hides input, which is not
  followed at all, as the GUI puts its text in the hidden-input box a frontend with no window does not have;
  unknown, with errorString(), for a name that is not a label's and an href that is not one of its links as its
  text holds them now; refused where runLua() is.
- docs/headless.md describes it in "Embedding it: the windows scripts make".

Tested in HeadlessSessionWindowsTest (each scheme, aliases, a Lua error, a scheme not run, a prompt: link while
the game hides input, the refusals, links with a raw < in the href or a space after the tag's <, the visited restyle
and clearVisitedLinks(), and a link whose Lua deletes its label). LabelAnchorInteractionTest covers the desktop's
clicks as before.

Carried by Mudlet/android's scripts/apply-mudlet-patches.sh until Mudlet/Mudlet has it.
Upstream: not opened yet

